Real defects:

- **P1 — The bare root commit is classified but omitted from review.** `_gate_floor_paths()` explicitly adds the root commit’s own files when no validated baseline exists ([bin/coverloop:483](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:483)), but `cmd_check()` discards `prior_validated` and reviews `root..HEAD`, which excludes everything introduced by the root commit ([bin/coverloop:2466](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2466), [bin/coverloop:2471](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2471)). A root-commit migration followed by another commit derives L3, yet both reviewers receive a packet without the migration and can authorize the entire span.

- **P1 — Self-attested ancestors can suppress mandatory independent reviews.** Baseline validation calls `evaluate()` without `require_captured=True` ([bin/coverloop:392](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:392)); self-attested passes are rejected only when that flag is enabled ([bin/coverloop:1613](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1613)). Therefore an ancestor recorded through `attest --codex pass --glm pass --approve ...` becomes a validated baseline without either reviewer transcript. A later L1 change starts after that baseline, and `cmd_check()` schedules no reviewer below L2 ([bin/coverloop:2502](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2502)). This bypasses the new command’s independent-review guarantee.

- **P1 — The repository can weaken its own test gate without triggering review.** `check` runs the current, repository-controlled `test_command` ([bin/coverloop:1375](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1375)), while `.coverloop/config.json` falls through to L1 and reviewers run only at L2/L3 ([bin/coverloop:531](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:531), [bin/coverloop:2502](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2502)). A config-only commit changing the command to `true` consequently runs no meaningful tests, receives no independent review, and can print `SAFE TO MERGE`.

- **P1 — CI does not execute any newly added v2.11 regression tests.** `unittest.main()` runs before `TenthRoundDerivedTierAndCheck` is defined ([tests/test_properties.py:1851](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/tests/test_properties.py:1851), [tests/test_properties.py:1855](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/tests/test_properties.py:1855)), and CI invokes the file directly ([.github/workflows/test.yml:40](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/.github/workflows/test.yml:40)). The entire new class is therefore absent from CI discovery.

- **P2 — `check` produces a malformed patch artifact.** The shared git wrapper strips the diff’s final newline ([bin/coverloop:618](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:618)), and `cmd_check()` writes that stripped result as `COVERLOOP_DIFF` ([bin/coverloop:2472](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2472)). The supplied artifact reproduces this: `git apply --stat` reports `corrupt patch at line 1956`, while the direct Git diff parses successfully. Patch-based reviewers will fail or be unable to reconstruct the change.

- **P2 — `_validated_baseline()` has inconsistent return arity.** Error/shallow paths return three values ([bin/coverloop:354](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:354)), while the success path returns two ([bin/coverloop:397](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:397)) and callers unpack two ([bin/coverloop:463](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:463)). Top-level callers generally fail closed, but through an unintended exception and generic error instead of the designed shallow-history path.

Style-only observations: none.

